      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "```js\nconst TUNING = {\n  car: {\n    maxSpeed: 62,        // m/s top speed without boost\n    accel: 14,           // m/s² engine\n    brake: 30,           // m/s² braking\n    drag: 0.0021,        // 1/m, decel = drag*v*v\n    rolling: 0.6,        // m/s² constant coast decel\n    reverseSpeed: 12,    // m/s\n    steerRate: 2.4,      // rad/s yaw at low speed\n    steerAtSpeed: 0.5,   // fraction of steerRate left at maxSpeed (linear blend)\n    grip: 9,             // 1/s lateral-velocity damping\n    driftGrip: 2.2,      // 1/s while drifting\n    driftSteer: 1.5,     // steer multiplier while drifting\n    driftMinSpeed: 18,   // m/s needed to start/keep a drift\n    driftDrag: 1.2,      // m/s² extra decel while sliding\n    boostFill: 0.34,     // meter (0..1) per s of drift\n    boostSpeed: 78,      // m/s cap while boosting\n    boostAccel: 22,      // m/s² extra push while boosting\n    boostSeconds: 2,     // s for a full meter\n    wallSlow: 0.55,      // speed multiplier on wall hit\n    bump: 6              // m/s impulse car-to-car\n  },\n  ai: [\n    { name: \"VOLT\",   color: \"#ff2bd6\", skill: 0.99, aggression: 0.8 },\n    { name: \"NOVA\",   color: \"#00f0ff\", skill: 0.97, aggression: 0.5 },\n    { name: \"HEX\",    color: \"#b26bff\", skill: 0.94, aggression: 0.7 },\n    { name: \"LUMEN\",  color: \"#ffe14d\", skill: 0.91, aggression: 0.3 },\n    { name: \"RAZOR\",  color: \"#39ff7a\", skill: 0.87, aggression: 0.9 }\n  ],\n  race: {\n    laps: 3,\n    countdown: 3,          // s, shows 3-2-1-GO\n    checkpoints: 24,       // ~75 m apart on 1.8 km\n    wrongWaySeconds: 1.5,  // s before warning shows\n    aiLatAccel: 17,        // m/s², AI corner speed = sqrt(aiLatAccel*radius)\n    aiBrakeLook: 60,       // m, AI looks ahead this far to brake\n    rubberBand: { range: 120, ahead: 0.95, behind: 1.06 } // m gap, speed multipliers\n  },\n  camera: {\n    distance: 7.5,   // m behind\n    height: 2.8,     // m above\n    lag: 0.12,       // s smoothing time constant\n    fov: 70,         // deg base\n    fovBoost: 12     // deg added while boosting\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Notes**\n\n1. Race flow: on the title screen, Enter, a click or a tap on START moves to the countdown. Cars are frozen for 3-2-1, then GO starts the race clock. When the player finishes lap 3, the game goes to results. The podium appears once all rivals have finished or 8 s have passed (unfinished rivals are ranked by progress), and Race again resets to the countdown.\n2. Starting a drift: hold Space while steering at 18 m/s or more. Lateral grip drops to `driftGrip`, steering is multiplied by `driftSteer`, and the boost meter fills by `boostFill` each second.\n3. Ending a drift: the drift ends when Space is released, the car falls below `driftMinSpeed`, or it hits a wall. A wall hit ends the drift and keeps the meter.\n4. Boost: Shift drains the meter over `boostSeconds` and raises the speed cap to `boostSpeed`. One full drift-and-boost cycle gains about 0.5–0.7 s, so 2–3 cycles per lap are clearly worth taking.\n5. Laps: checkpoints are counted only in order (next = (last+1) % 24). A lap counts when the car crosses checkpoint 0 after checkpoint 23, so shortcuts and reversing gain nothing. Lap time and best-lap time are taken at that crossing.\n6. Positions: cars are ranked every frame by progress = lap*24 + checkpoint + the fraction of the distance to the next checkpoint along the centreline.\n7. Wrong way: if the car's heading points more than 100° away from the track direction at 5 m/s or more for `wrongWaySeconds`, show WRONG WAY. It clears when the car is back within 100°.\n8. Pacing has not been verified: this is a calculated estimate (average ≈33 m/s gives a 54 s lap on 1.8 km, with rivals about 1–4 s behind a clean player) and still needs a playtest in the built game."
