      "output": "**Review record: not actually run**\n\nThis is a static reading of the delivered HTML only. Nothing was loaded in a browser, so rendering, frame rate, audio, touch behaviour and pacing are untested.\n\n**Confirmed in the source**\n- **Tuning:** the `TUNING` values match the upstream block exactly; only the comments were removed. The other modules and wiring look complete and consistent, but they could not be compared with upstream copies.\n- **External requests:** the only one is `three.js/r128/three.min.js` from cdnjs. There are no fonts, fetches or other URLs.\n- **Drift and boost:**\n  - A drift starts with Space, speed of at least 18 m/s and steering above 0.2.\n  - Grip drops to `driftGrip`, steering is multiplied by `driftSteer`, and the meter fills by `boostFill` each second.\n  - Boost drains over 2 s and raises the cap to 78 m/s.\n- **Laps and positions:**\n  - Checkpoints are counted only in order (`cs===nx`).\n  - The first crossing of checkpoint 0 only arms `go`; later crossings count a lap and record lap and best-lap times.\n  - Reversing freezes progress.\n  - Ranking puts finished cars first by finish time, then the rest by progress.\n- **Wrong way:** shows at more than 100° off the track direction (`dot<-.17`), above 5 m/s, after 1.5 s, and clears immediately.\n- **Countdown:** cars are frozen for 3-2-1, the clock resets at GO, and GO is shown.\n- **Results:** they appear when all cars finish or after 8 s, and unfinished rivals are listed as DNF in progress order. RACE AGAIN (or Enter) rebuilds the cars and returns to the countdown.\n- **AI:**\n  - Corner speed follows `sqrt(aiLatAccel/k)`, with a 60 m braking look-ahead.\n  - Each rival's skill scales its pace, and rubber-banding uses the tuned values.\n  - Rivals move sideways around a car ahead to overtake.\n- **Touch:** on-screen left, right, drift, boost, brake and gas buttons use pointer events and appear on touch devices.\n- **Language:** all text is in English.\n\n**Defects found**\n1. **A wall hit does not really end a drift.** `nrRoad` sets `c.drift=false`, but `nrPhys` restarts it on the next frame whenever Space is held and the player is steering: `c.drift=!!(inp.drift&&vF>=T.driftMinSpeed&&(c.drift||Math.abs(st)>.2))`.\n2. **The bump impulse is far below the tuned value.** The code gives `k=-vr*.6+b*.15`, so the base push is 0.9 m/s instead of the tuned 6 m/s.\n3. **The AI line is not a full racing line.** The offset `Math.sign(kk)*…*(q.w-2.5)` moves rivals toward the inside of a corner only, with no outside–inside–outside path.\n4. **The start button is labelled RACE, not START** as the race-flow note says.\n5. **The results screen is a ranked list, not a podium.**\n6. **The engine and music keep playing on the results screen,** because `engine(false)` and `music(false)` are never called.\n7. **The touch controls stay visible over the title and results screens.**\n8. **`checkTrack()` is never called** and `TRACK.checkpoints` is never used, so the layout is not checked for overlaps or tower clearance.\n\n**Unverified items**\n- Rendering: the city, sun, grid, banked corners, tunnel, light bars and trails.\n- Whether the track is about 1.8 km long, and whether it is free of overlaps.\n- Pacing: the 54 s lap estimate, rivals finishing 1–4 s behind, and the 0.5–0.7 s gain from each drift-and-boost cycle.\n- Whether rivals ever drift or boost, since their drift threshold needs a corner radius under 30 m.\n- Wall scrape feel, how bumps feel in play, and whether overtakes actually happen.\n- Touch and multitouch on real devices, and audio unlocking in the browser.\n- Performance and console errors in an actual run."
